From 0814a922403a7c6ab01a14482ed66565c6b8b9c6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gki <gki@localhost>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 00:47:37 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 83/83] arm64: gki_defconfig: align monolithic image with
 Haruhi config

D class (ours=m -> Haruhi=y): 81 symbols set to =y (80 effective;
ZSMALLOC stays m, selected by ZRAM=m, hidden when ZSWAP=n).
A class (Haruhi-only, enabled here): LTO/LTO_CLANG/LTO_CLANG_THIN,
AUTOFDO_CLANG, CFI_PERMISSIVE, IDLE_PAGE_TRACKING,
TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_ALWAYS, TMPFS_POSIX_ACL, TMPFS_XATTR,
RCU_NOCB_CPU_DEFAULT_ALL, TASKS_TRACE_RCU_READ_MB,
PCIEASPM_POWER_SUPERSAVE, WQ_POWER_EFFICIENT_DEFAULT (13 effective).
Blocked by deps (not set): OPTPROBES (arm64 has no HAVE_OPTPROBES),
ZPOOL (only ZSWAP selects it; ZSWAP=n), MODULE_SCMVERSION
(needs LOCALVERSION_AUTO, kept off for stock vermagic).
Mutual exclusions resolved: LTO_NONE, TRANSPARENT_HUGEPAGE_MADVISE,
PCIEASPM_DEFAULT all off.
